course: dictionary
lesson: 8179
title: Respect: a feeling, an action, a phrase
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Respect can be a noun or a verb. As a noun it is a feeling: someone or something is important and should be treated well. As a verb it is an action: to respect someone is to treat them politely and fairly and value their feelings and choices.
explain: «I respect Sam.» Here respect is a verb, so the speaker is saying Sam is someone to treat well. To respect a rule or a place means to follow it or take care of it, so «respect the park» means keep it clean and safe.
explain: Respect also appears in set phrases. «Show respect» and «treat with respect» are things you do. «Pay your respects» means visit or honour someone, often after a death. Read the words around respect to find which meaning fits.
fact: Respect means a feeling that someone or something is important and should be treated well.
fact: To respect someone is to treat them politely and fairly and value their feelings and choices.
fact: «In this respect» means in this way or in this detail.
fact: «Respect means being curious and kind: asking polite questions, saying «Happy Diwali» or «Eid Mubarak», and never laughing at someone's food, clothes or customs.»
fact: «You don't have to be friends to treat someone with respect.»
exercise: «I respect Sam.» In this sentence, what kind of word is respect? | A noun, a name for a thing | A pronoun, a word that stands in for a name | *A verb, an action word | An adjective, a describing word
exercise: Ruby says, «Be sure to respect the park by leaving no litter.» What does respect mean here? | Ignore it and walk past it | Paint it a bright colour | *Follow it and take care of it | Break it on purpose
exercise: Which phrase means visit or honour someone, often after a death? | show respect | *pay your respects | earn respect | with respect
test: «At festive dinners even kids raise their juice and shout gānbēi! (cheers!), holding the glass a little lower than an elder's, a small, lovely sign of respect.» What does the lower glass show? | A glass that is broken | *Respect for an elder | Anger at the adults | Thirst for more juice
test: Which action is a way to show respect to other people? | Interrupting people when they talk | Laughing at someone's clothes | Touching other people's things without asking | *Listening when others speak
exam: Which sentence uses respect as a feeling? | *«He has deep respect for his grandad.» | «They respected the rules and went home.» | «She walked the dog and ate her lunch.»
